     - \(3^{-1} \mod 16\): We need \(3b \equiv 1 \mod 16\). Testing values, we find \(3 \cdot 11 \equiv 33 \equiv 1 \mod 16\), so \(3^{-1} \equiv 11\).
     - \(5^{-1} \mod 16\): Testing values, we find \(5 \cdot 13 \equiv 65 \equiv 1 \mod 16\), so \(5^{-1} \equiv 13\).
     - \(7^{-1} \mod 16\): Testing values, we find \(7 \cdot 7 \equiv 49 \equiv 1 \mod 16\), so \(7^{-1} \equiv 7\).
     - \(9^{-1} \mod 16\): Testing values, we find \(9 \cdot 9 \equiv 81 \equiv 1 \mod 16\), so \(9^{-1} \equiv 9\).
     - \(11^{-1} \mod 16\): Testing values, we find \(11 \cdot 3 \equiv 33 \equiv 1 \mod 16\), so \(11^{-1} \equiv 3\).
     - \(13^{-1} \mod 16\): Testing values, we find \(13 \cdot 5 \equiv 65 \equiv 1 \mod 16\), so \(13^{-1} \equiv 5\).
