3. \( \cos^2 x + \sin x \cos x > \sin^2 x \)

Using the identity \( \sin^2 x + \cos^2 x = 1 \), we can simplify the inequalities:
1. \( 1 > \sin x \cos x \)
2. \( \sin^2 x + \sin x \cos x > \cos^2 x \)
3. \( \cos^2 x + \sin x \cos x > \sin^2 x \)

