The direction vector \(\mathbf{d}\) can be calculated as the difference between the two vectors:

\[
\mathbf{d} = \mathbf{b} - \mathbf{a}.
\]

Now, we perform the subtraction component-wise:

\[
\mathbf{d} = \begin{pmatrix} -11 \\ 1 \\ 28 \end{pmatrix} - \begin{pmatrix} 5 \\ -3 \\ -4 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -11 - 5 \\ 1 - (-3) \\ 28 - (-4) \end{pmatrix}.
