   \[
   \text{proj}_{\mathbf{v}} \mathbf{u} = \frac{\mathbf{u} \cdot \mathbf{v}}{\mathbf{v} \cdot \mathbf{v}} \mathbf{v}
   \]
   The projection matrix \(P\) can be derived from this formula. The projection matrix \(P\) onto a vector \(\mathbf{v}\) is given by:
